1
00:00:29,404 --> 00:00:31,948
This man snuck into the castle town.

2
00:00:32,032 --> 00:00:33,199
And over and over,

3
00:00:33,783 --> 00:00:35,994
he stole food and valuables.

4
00:00:36,077 --> 00:00:37,245
A petty thief!

5
00:00:38,538 --> 00:00:41,207
What's worse,
we found this in his possession.

6
00:00:44,002 --> 00:00:45,628
Yes, he's a ninja.

7
00:00:45,712 --> 00:00:49,716
He hid his name and background
to inflict crime and violence upon us all.

8
00:00:53,595 --> 00:00:57,015
Thus, he is sentenced to death!

9
00:00:57,098 --> 00:00:58,308
Yes, sir!

10
00:01:00,602 --> 00:01:02,687
Get him!

11
00:01:02,771 --> 00:01:04,147
Get to it already…

12
00:01:04,230 --> 00:01:05,356
Kill him!

13
00:01:05,440 --> 00:01:06,900
Get him!

14
00:01:07,609 --> 00:01:09,152
Get to it already!

15
00:01:10,153 --> 00:01:11,446
This world is rotten,

16
00:01:12,781 --> 00:01:14,657
and I'm sick of living in it!

17
00:01:18,411 --> 00:01:19,788
SASUKE

18
00:01:19,871 --> 00:01:22,415
On second thought, I'm really sorry.

19
00:01:22,499 --> 00:01:25,001
-Kill him! Kill him!
-Please, no!

20
00:01:32,550 --> 00:01:33,802
Just kidding!

21
00:01:33,885 --> 00:01:35,136
Oh, and I'm taking this.

22
00:01:37,639 --> 00:01:38,598
And this.

23
00:01:38,681 --> 00:01:40,558
Kill him! Now!

24
00:01:50,443 --> 00:01:54,197
After him!
Don't let him escape! He must die!

25
00:02:14,509 --> 00:02:18,805
Please don't! I'm begging you!
Spare me, please!

26
00:02:24,102 --> 00:02:27,856
I've got nothing against thieves,
but you can't steal from a girl.

27
00:02:27,939 --> 00:02:28,940
Get him!

28
00:02:34,863 --> 00:02:35,905
Punk!

29
00:02:43,204 --> 00:02:44,080
Hey!

30
00:02:44,956 --> 00:02:45,915
Stop, or she dies!

31
00:02:54,007 --> 00:02:55,300
Good night.

32
00:02:59,137 --> 00:03:00,054
Sir…

33
00:03:01,306 --> 00:03:02,807
Thank you so much.

34
00:03:04,475 --> 00:03:06,185
If there's a girl in need of help,

35
00:03:07,353 --> 00:03:09,063
helping her is the obvious thing to do.

36
00:03:10,189 --> 00:03:12,942
OKUNI

37
00:03:13,568 --> 00:03:16,279
So, what do you say
we get some <i>dango</i> at a teahouse?

38
00:03:17,780 --> 00:03:19,616
-Actually…
-Do you dislike <i>dango?</i>

39
00:03:19,699 --> 00:03:20,992
No, that's not it.

40
00:03:31,628 --> 00:03:32,921
Ninja?

41
00:03:33,004 --> 00:03:35,715
That's as far as you go. Turn yourself in.

42
00:03:35,798 --> 00:03:39,719
You know,
I just hate being ordered around.

43
00:03:42,889 --> 00:03:44,182
-Get ready to fly.
-What?

44
00:04:22,553 --> 00:04:24,222
Not again.

45
00:04:25,598 --> 00:04:26,849
I'm Okuni.

46
00:04:27,725 --> 00:04:28,851
What's your name?

47
00:04:32,105 --> 00:04:33,106
Who, me?

48
00:04:34,357 --> 00:04:36,359
Neither moats nor castle walls
mean anything to me.

49
00:04:37,151 --> 00:04:38,987
The best in the east, the ninja of flight.

50
00:04:39,612 --> 00:04:41,572
The name's Sasuke.

51
00:04:43,866 --> 00:04:45,785
So how about those <i>dango?</i>

52
00:04:47,161 --> 00:04:48,705
-Sure.
-Really?

53
00:04:48,788 --> 00:04:49,747
It'd be my pleasure.

54
00:04:50,790 --> 00:04:52,125
Hooray!

55
00:04:58,548 --> 00:05:01,009
These guys are so persistent.

56
00:05:01,676 --> 00:05:02,760
Let's go!

57
00:05:08,224 --> 00:05:09,350
Poison…

58
00:05:12,770 --> 00:05:14,063
Are you all right?

59
00:05:14,147 --> 00:05:15,148
Run.

60
00:05:15,940 --> 00:05:16,899
Yes.

61
00:05:41,090 --> 00:05:43,885
Shield, Sanctuary, Strike, Flame Release!

62
00:05:43,968 --> 00:05:45,094
FLAME RELEASE

63
00:06:24,383 --> 00:06:25,718
My rice balls

64
00:06:26,344 --> 00:06:27,929
are delicious, you know.

65
00:06:44,112 --> 00:06:45,071
He's awake!

66
00:06:45,154 --> 00:06:46,447
Master Hakuunsai!

67
00:06:49,492 --> 00:06:51,452
It's been five years, Sasuke.

68
00:06:51,536 --> 00:06:52,370
HAKUUNSAI

69
00:06:52,453 --> 00:06:53,663
Old man.

70
00:06:54,330 --> 00:06:57,208
You've sunk so low you've become a bandit.

71
00:06:58,209 --> 00:06:59,710
You just had to stick your nose in.

72
00:07:00,211 --> 00:07:01,629
What are you trying to pull?

73
00:07:02,296 --> 00:07:03,464
I thought

74
00:07:04,340 --> 00:07:05,842
I'd knock some sense into you.

75
00:07:06,342 --> 00:07:08,803
How I live my life is my business.

76
00:07:08,886 --> 00:07:11,431
-Here. Eat up.
-No, thanks.

77
00:07:13,724 --> 00:07:16,436
Your pickled plums are too sour.

78
00:07:16,519 --> 00:07:18,312
Grandpa, it's time to train.

79
00:07:18,396 --> 00:07:19,689
Coming.

80
00:07:20,273 --> 00:07:22,608
-Wanna join us, mister?
-"Mister"?

81
00:07:23,192 --> 00:07:24,402
Who's this brat?

82
00:07:24,485 --> 00:07:25,778
Kids just like you.

83
00:07:26,946 --> 00:07:28,698
They're all orphans.

84
00:07:30,032 --> 00:07:32,410
Are you still doing this?

85
00:07:32,493 --> 00:07:33,786
Even though you're broke?

86
00:07:35,413 --> 00:07:38,833
And you're still using
those beat-up <i>shuriken?</i>

87
00:07:40,585 --> 00:07:44,255
Listen. You'll never get strong
staying in a dump like this.

88
00:07:47,550 --> 00:07:50,344
Do yourself a favor
and get out while you can.

89
00:07:52,346 --> 00:07:54,182
Well, I'm off.

90
00:07:54,974 --> 00:07:56,142
Wait.

91
00:07:57,143 --> 00:07:59,228
Not until you beat me.

92
00:07:59,312 --> 00:08:01,439
Don't push yourself, old man.

93
00:08:01,522 --> 00:08:03,983
There's no way I'd lose to a mere thief.

94
00:08:05,151 --> 00:08:08,571
What's the difference
between a thief and a ninja?

95
00:08:09,989 --> 00:08:12,116
A ninja who serves no lord

96
00:08:13,034 --> 00:08:14,660
is just a thief.

97
00:08:16,412 --> 00:08:18,414
You're the only one

98
00:08:19,332 --> 00:08:20,416
saying that bullshit!

99
00:08:35,389 --> 00:08:37,433
I'd rather die

100
00:08:38,142 --> 00:08:39,936
than live bowing to anyone!

101
00:08:43,147 --> 00:08:45,107
No matter how hard I train…

102
00:08:46,943 --> 00:08:49,153
or how much I hone my skills,

103
00:08:50,738 --> 00:08:52,532
people still look down on us

104
00:08:53,741 --> 00:08:55,076
and mock us

105
00:08:55,826 --> 00:08:57,203
just for being ninjas!

106
00:09:00,748 --> 00:09:02,667
I'll use my power

107
00:09:03,793 --> 00:09:05,753
to live as I please

108
00:09:05,836 --> 00:09:08,256
and take whatever I want!

109
00:09:16,264 --> 00:09:17,265
Your strength

110
00:09:18,516 --> 00:09:21,727
is meant to serve others.

111
00:09:23,229 --> 00:09:24,355
Others?

112
00:09:25,565 --> 00:09:28,442
What have they ever done for me?

113
00:09:35,866 --> 00:09:38,494
You've grown old, Hakuunsai.

114
00:09:38,578 --> 00:09:42,123
Is bowing your head really so unbearable?

115
00:09:50,673 --> 00:09:52,633
Conceal, Secure, Bind, Switch!

116
00:09:52,717 --> 00:09:53,718
SWITCH

117
00:09:57,805 --> 00:09:59,307
-Body Switch!
-Body Switch!

118
00:10:01,642 --> 00:10:03,728
So you finally bowed your head.

119
00:10:03,811 --> 00:10:05,313
Damn it…

120
00:10:06,606 --> 00:10:08,065
Sasuke.

121
00:10:08,858 --> 00:10:10,651
Even in a world like this,

122
00:10:12,737 --> 00:10:14,488
there are still good people.

123
00:10:22,496 --> 00:10:24,749
Still can't keep your hands
to yourself, huh?

124
00:10:25,666 --> 00:10:27,001
It's probably cheap junk, anyway.

125
00:10:28,002 --> 00:10:29,587
This sword…

126
00:10:34,800 --> 00:10:36,927
is the cursed blade Muramasa.

127
00:10:38,095 --> 00:10:39,096
A cursed blade?

128
00:10:40,222 --> 00:10:44,977
It's said to bring misfortune
to Tokugawa Ieyasu and his clan.

129
00:10:45,978 --> 00:10:46,854
That's why

130
00:10:47,438 --> 00:10:51,484
it's considered a protective blade
by those who oppose the Tokugawa.

131
00:10:52,777 --> 00:10:54,695
Lord Sanada Masayuki gave it to me

132
00:10:55,237 --> 00:10:57,907
as a reward for the Battle of Ueda.

133
00:10:58,449 --> 00:11:00,076
The Battle of Ueda?

134
00:11:01,494 --> 00:11:02,536
Sanada?

135
00:11:03,829 --> 00:11:06,791
You don't know? The legendary Sanada clan
and their Ten Braves.

136
00:11:07,416 --> 00:11:08,417
What?

137
00:11:09,085 --> 00:11:10,086
Well, then…

138
00:11:11,128 --> 00:11:12,755
<i>The year is 1600.</i>

139
00:11:13,422 --> 00:11:14,882
<i>Fourteen years ago,</i>

140
00:11:15,800 --> 00:11:18,844
<i>a great battle was fought</i>
<i>that would divide Japan into two.</i>

141
00:11:18,928 --> 00:11:20,096
TOKUGAWA ARMY - SANADA ARMY

142
00:11:20,179 --> 00:11:23,015
<i>Against the Eastern Army</i>
<i>led by Tokugawa Ieyasu,</i>

143
00:11:23,099 --> 00:11:26,227
<i>the Sanada clan barricaded themselves</i>
<i>inside Ueda Castle in Shinano Province,</i>

144
00:11:26,936 --> 00:11:29,939
<i>where they faced the forces of Hidetada,</i>
<i>Ieyasu's eldest son,</i>

145
00:11:30,606 --> 00:11:33,192
<i>as he marched to the decisive</i>
<i>Battle of Sekigahara.</i>

146
00:11:33,901 --> 00:11:35,694
<i>Their forces outnumbered</i>
<i>the Sanada, 20 to 1.</i>

147
00:11:36,404 --> 00:11:39,323
<i>Hidetada was certain of victory,</i>

148
00:11:39,407 --> 00:11:43,202
<i>but Lord Sanada Masayuki</i>
<i>was lying in wait.</i>

149
00:11:43,285 --> 00:11:44,161
HAKUUNSAI

150
00:11:45,329 --> 00:11:48,332
<i>A sudden flood</i>
<i>swept away Hidetada's troops,</i>

151
00:11:49,542 --> 00:11:53,379
<i>then Masayuki's son, Lord Nobushige,</i>
<i>launched a surprise attack.</i>

152
00:11:53,462 --> 00:11:54,588
SANADA NOBUSHIGE

153
00:11:54,672 --> 00:12:00,219
<i>Next, a mighty arrow from master archer</i>
<i>Unno Rokuro pierced the enemy ranks,</i>

154
00:12:00,302 --> 00:12:02,263
<i>throwing Hidetada's army into chaos.</i>

155
00:12:02,888 --> 00:12:04,890
<i>As a thick fog shrouded the battlefield,</i>

156
00:12:05,516 --> 00:12:07,726
<i>the Sanada Braves,</i>

157
00:12:07,810 --> 00:12:11,021
<i>masters of ninjutsu and martial arts,</i>
<i>struck one after another.</i>

158
00:12:11,772 --> 00:12:14,650
<i>The young genius, Kirigakure Saizo.</i>

159
00:12:15,317 --> 00:12:18,320
<i>Master of the chain-sickle,</i>
<i>Yuri Kamanosuke.</i>

160
00:12:20,614 --> 00:12:22,658
<i>The strongman, Miyoshi Isa.</i>

161
00:12:24,368 --> 00:12:26,954
<i>The poison expert, Miyoshi Seikai.</i>

162
00:12:28,998 --> 00:12:31,834
<i>The loyal warrior, Mochizuki Rokuro.</i>

163
00:12:32,793 --> 00:12:35,296
<i>The strategist, Anayama Kosuke.</i>

164
00:12:36,213 --> 00:12:39,800
<i>The ninja of a hundred skills,</i>
<i>Nezu Jinpachi.</i>

165
00:12:40,718 --> 00:12:43,387
<i>Through the cunning</i>
<i>of Sanada Masayuki and Nobushige,</i>

166
00:12:43,471 --> 00:12:46,724
<i>and the brave warriors' fierce resistance,</i>
<i>Hidetada's army was routed.</i>

167
00:12:47,725 --> 00:12:49,268
<i>They never made it</i>

168
00:12:50,102 --> 00:12:53,647
<i>to the decisive</i>
<i>Battle of Sekigahara in time.</i>

169
00:12:55,274 --> 00:12:57,526
<i>Despite the Sanada clan's valiant efforts,</i>

170
00:12:58,235 --> 00:13:01,489
the Tokugawa emerged victorious.

171
00:13:02,364 --> 00:13:03,240
But…

172
00:13:03,908 --> 00:13:07,286
-You disgrace us!
<i>-…Ieyasu's fury was said to be immense.</i>

173
00:13:07,369 --> 00:13:08,329
Father.

174
00:13:09,205 --> 00:13:10,623
Forgive me!

175
00:13:10,706 --> 00:13:11,832
Damn it…

176
00:13:11,916 --> 00:13:12,791
TOKUGAWA IEYASU

177
00:13:12,875 --> 00:13:14,293
Those Sanada!

178
00:13:14,376 --> 00:13:16,712
<i>The Tokugawa had lost</i>
<i>to the Sanada before.</i>

179
00:13:16,795 --> 00:13:18,631
<i>This was their second humiliation.</i>

180
00:13:19,215 --> 00:13:21,717
<i>-And so, having incurred…</i>
-I'll curse them for all eternity!

181
00:13:21,800 --> 00:13:24,553
<i>…Ieyasu's wrath,</i>
<i>Lord Masayuki and Lord Nobushige</i>

182
00:13:25,179 --> 00:13:26,639
<i>were ordered into confinement</i>

183
00:13:27,223 --> 00:13:30,351
<i>and placed under strict surveillance.</i>

184
00:13:31,185 --> 00:13:32,353
What a load of crap.

185
00:13:33,479 --> 00:13:34,855
The Sanada Braves?

186
00:13:35,731 --> 00:13:38,150
I doubt guys that strong ever existed.

187
00:13:38,234 --> 00:13:40,194
They were strong indeed.

188
00:13:41,070 --> 00:13:43,614
Far stronger than you'll ever be.

189
00:13:44,823 --> 00:13:48,077
Because they fought
out of loyalty to their lord.

190
00:13:51,664 --> 00:13:53,249
You can have this sword.

191
00:13:55,543 --> 00:13:56,377
Come on!

192
00:13:56,460 --> 00:13:57,753
Let's eat.

193
00:13:58,629 --> 00:13:59,713
You're hungry, aren't you?

194
00:14:01,715 --> 00:14:02,758
Not really.

195
00:14:06,095 --> 00:14:08,597
I can tell when you're lying.

196
00:14:11,892 --> 00:14:13,143
Got anywhere to go back to?

197
00:14:17,731 --> 00:14:20,109
Look, I made it so well!

198
00:14:20,192 --> 00:14:22,444
-That's very good.
-What's that?

199
00:14:22,528 --> 00:14:24,488
-Plum.
-Oh, plum.

200
00:14:38,586 --> 00:14:39,545
Hey, Grandpa.

201
00:14:40,212 --> 00:14:42,590
What happened to Lord Sanada after that?

202
00:14:42,673 --> 00:14:43,883
Who knows?

203
00:14:45,009 --> 00:14:46,719
I wonder how he's doing.

204
00:14:59,815 --> 00:15:01,233
You've had too much to drink.

205
00:15:01,317 --> 00:15:03,986
KUDOYAMA VILLAGE

206
00:15:05,404 --> 00:15:06,488
What brings you here?

207
00:15:07,489 --> 00:15:10,200
I've come to pay my respects
to Lord Sanada Masayuki.

208
00:15:10,284 --> 00:15:12,077
KUDOYAMA VILLAGE
TRAVEL PASS

209
00:15:12,161 --> 00:15:14,246
THIS PERSON IS AUTHORIZED
TO TRAVEL WITHOUT HINDRANCE

210
00:15:14,330 --> 00:15:15,581
All right. You can pass.

211
00:15:33,265 --> 00:15:34,099
Wait!

212
00:15:44,193 --> 00:15:45,569
SHUTO KAGEAKI

213
00:15:45,653 --> 00:15:46,654
Go.

214
00:16:38,998 --> 00:16:39,999
Father.

215
00:16:40,833 --> 00:16:43,585
The pickled plums
turned out delicious again this year.

216
00:16:49,508 --> 00:16:55,431
Even after defeating Ieyasu twice…

217
00:17:03,522 --> 00:17:04,898
This bitter regret…

218
00:17:06,025 --> 00:17:08,861
You must avenge me.

219
00:17:11,155 --> 00:17:12,156
Father.

220
00:17:25,961 --> 00:17:29,048
SANADA YUKIMURA

221
00:17:29,131 --> 00:17:30,424
My lord.

222
00:17:31,091 --> 00:17:34,428
A traveling monk
has come to pay his respects.

223
00:17:34,511 --> 00:17:37,806
I am Sojun,
a monk traveling across the land.

224
00:17:37,890 --> 00:17:41,018
You must be Lord Nobushige.

225
00:17:41,727 --> 00:17:43,729
I go by Yukimura now.

226
00:17:44,938 --> 00:17:47,566
You've taken the "Yuki"
from your father's name.

227
00:17:48,192 --> 00:17:49,026
Yes.

228
00:17:50,944 --> 00:17:52,863
I've come on behalf of the Toyotomi.

229
00:17:52,946 --> 00:17:53,989
The Toyotomi?!

230
00:17:54,573 --> 00:17:55,783
This is my son, Daisuke.

231
00:17:57,576 --> 00:17:58,577
I see.

232
00:17:59,203 --> 00:18:00,245
And?

233
00:18:01,789 --> 00:18:03,415
Ieyasu has finally declared his intent

234
00:18:04,041 --> 00:18:06,335
to destroy the Toyotomi.

235
00:18:09,004 --> 00:18:09,963
Please take a look.

236
00:18:14,718 --> 00:18:16,595
This is the inscription on the bell

237
00:18:17,262 --> 00:18:21,183
dedicated by Lord Hideyori and Lady Yodo
upon the reconstruction of Hokoji Temple.

238
00:18:21,266 --> 00:18:22,351
MAY THE NATION BE PEACEFUL

239
00:18:23,811 --> 00:18:25,687
It means the realm will be at peace,

240
00:18:25,771 --> 00:18:29,441
and everyone from the ruler
to the common people

241
00:18:30,109 --> 00:18:32,027
will live in prosperity and happiness.

242
00:18:33,278 --> 00:18:35,030
But Lord Ieyasu interpreted it

243
00:18:36,198 --> 00:18:38,450
as splitting his name in two

244
00:18:38,534 --> 00:18:41,787
and proclaiming the Toyotomi
as the rightful rulers.

245
00:18:42,788 --> 00:18:45,332
So he took it as an insult
to the Tokugawa?

246
00:18:45,457 --> 00:18:49,002
Yes. He was absolutely furious.

247
00:18:51,630 --> 00:18:54,716
The Toyotomi need your strength now
more than ever, Lord Yukimura.

248
00:18:54,800 --> 00:18:59,805
Please, return to Osaka
for the sake of the Toyotomi clan.

249
00:19:03,433 --> 00:19:06,854
Lady Yodo sent me a letter as well,
asking me to come to her aid.

250
00:19:07,938 --> 00:19:08,772
Then…

251
00:19:09,356 --> 00:19:10,607
I'm afraid I must refuse.

252
00:19:11,692 --> 00:19:13,569
I've been confined here for 14 years.

253
00:19:14,153 --> 00:19:16,864
I no longer have the strength to wage war.

254
00:19:16,947 --> 00:19:20,492
What about the braves
who fought at the Battle of Ueda?

255
00:19:21,201 --> 00:19:23,203
They've all left my side.

256
00:19:24,496 --> 00:19:25,497
As you can see,

257
00:19:26,206 --> 00:19:28,375
only my son, Daisuke, remains.

258
00:19:29,668 --> 00:19:32,588
I've even sent my wife
back to our home province.

259
00:19:34,673 --> 00:19:37,467
I can never leave this village alive.

260
00:19:39,094 --> 00:19:42,139
Will you really waste away
in these mountains?

261
00:19:42,222 --> 00:19:46,435
You, the son of Lord Sanada Masayuki,
who defeated Tokugawa Ieyasu twice?

262
00:19:47,311 --> 00:19:48,645
Life here…

263
00:19:50,397 --> 00:19:51,690
isn't so bad.

264
00:20:12,336 --> 00:20:13,337
I wonder

265
00:20:14,254 --> 00:20:16,465
what's happening out there in the world.

266
00:20:17,341 --> 00:20:21,094
If you command me to,
I'll find out whether his story is true.

267
00:20:21,178 --> 00:20:23,222
KIRIGAKURE SAIZO

268
00:20:23,305 --> 00:20:24,598
No, leave it.

269
00:20:25,891 --> 00:20:27,893
I'm sorry, Saizo.

270
00:20:31,188 --> 00:20:32,564
Kill her!

271
00:20:33,106 --> 00:20:34,149
Please wait!

272
00:20:34,233 --> 00:20:35,359
What's going on?

273
00:20:36,568 --> 00:20:38,946
That woman was hiding rice

274
00:20:39,613 --> 00:20:41,782
to avoid paying her taxes.

275
00:20:41,865 --> 00:20:42,991
Get on with it!

276
00:20:43,075 --> 00:20:47,246
Would Lord Ieyasu really approve
of killing a peasant?

277
00:20:47,329 --> 00:20:48,705
Then as punishment,

278
00:20:49,414 --> 00:20:52,292
I'll raise this village's taxes by 30%.

279
00:20:53,126 --> 00:20:55,963
-But…
-Please. Just endure it for now.

280
00:20:56,046 --> 00:20:58,590
You can't even leave this village.

281
00:21:00,133 --> 00:21:01,843
What else can you do?

282
00:21:02,803 --> 00:21:04,179
This should be fun.

283
00:21:05,847 --> 00:21:06,890
Let's go!

284
00:21:08,433 --> 00:21:10,352
I'm sorry. This is all my fault.

285
00:21:11,311 --> 00:21:15,190
If it weren't for you, we'd be free
to come and go from the village.

286
00:21:16,608 --> 00:21:17,693
I'm sorry.

287
00:21:27,953 --> 00:21:31,581
-Damn it! Lost again.
-I'm on a lucky streak today.

288
00:21:31,665 --> 00:21:32,708
Here you go.

289
00:21:32,791 --> 00:21:34,584
YURI KAMANOSUKE

290
00:21:34,668 --> 00:21:38,005
MIYOSHI SEIKAI

291
00:21:41,842 --> 00:21:44,720
NEZU JINPACHI

292
00:21:45,304 --> 00:21:48,015
UNNO ROKURO

293
00:21:50,517 --> 00:21:54,146
Everyone's suffering,
and this is what we're stuck doing?

294
00:21:58,066 --> 00:21:59,818
MIYOSHI ISA

295
00:21:59,901 --> 00:22:00,902
Unno.

296
00:22:01,445 --> 00:22:04,781
I know how you feel,
but we have to endure it for now.

297
00:22:04,865 --> 00:22:05,699
MOCHIZUKI ROKURO

298
00:22:05,782 --> 00:22:07,701
If our true identities are discovered…

299
00:22:07,784 --> 00:22:08,618
ANAYAMA KOSUKE

300
00:22:08,702 --> 00:22:10,871
…it'll be the end of the Sanada clan
and this village.

301
00:22:12,831 --> 00:22:15,375
We've been told to endure it for 14 years.

302
00:22:16,918 --> 00:22:20,213
Hey, Mochizuki,
you've really turned into an old man.

303
00:22:20,297 --> 00:22:21,715
You haven't forgotten, have you?

304
00:22:22,466 --> 00:22:24,301
This is just a disguise.

305
00:22:27,012 --> 00:22:28,263
Hey! Are you listening, Isa?

306
00:22:30,057 --> 00:22:31,099
What?

307
00:22:34,603 --> 00:22:36,646
Think Lord Yukimura's holding up, too?

308
00:22:37,481 --> 00:22:39,274
He hasn't really gone soft, has he?

309
00:22:39,858 --> 00:22:41,026
Trust our lord.

310
00:22:42,694 --> 00:22:44,780
Haven't we always done that?

311
00:22:58,085 --> 00:23:00,587
TOKUGAWA HIDETADA

312
00:23:39,626 --> 00:23:40,544
You're back.

313
00:23:41,920 --> 00:23:42,838
Yes, my lord.

314
00:23:45,048 --> 00:23:46,007
What of the Sanada?

315
00:23:47,717 --> 00:23:49,845
Their fangs are gone.

316
00:23:49,928 --> 00:23:52,305
They're living like old men.

317
00:23:52,389 --> 00:23:54,141
I see, I see.

318
00:23:55,100 --> 00:23:56,643
Without his retainers,

319
00:23:57,561 --> 00:23:59,354
even a Sanada is just an ordinary man.

320
00:23:59,938 --> 00:24:00,814
My lord,

321
00:24:00,897 --> 00:24:04,317
that scheme with Hokoji Temple
was brilliant.

322
00:24:04,401 --> 00:24:07,362
That was Suden's scheme.

323
00:24:07,487 --> 00:24:12,117
As expected of Lord Konchiin,
the Tokugawa's brains.

324
00:24:12,993 --> 00:24:14,035
Well…

325
00:24:14,703 --> 00:24:17,831
It was all thanks
to the Great Shogun's wisdom

326
00:24:17,914 --> 00:24:20,500
in heeding my humble counsel.

327
00:24:20,584 --> 00:24:21,543
KONCHIIN SUDEN

328
00:24:26,089 --> 00:24:27,883
Sojun. Come closer.

329
00:24:28,675 --> 00:24:29,634
Yes, my lord.

330
00:24:30,635 --> 00:24:32,262
Your promised reward.

331
00:24:33,180 --> 00:24:35,140
The fabled elixir.

332
00:24:35,223 --> 00:24:37,142
Savor its power.

333
00:24:38,602 --> 00:24:39,936
I'm deeply grateful.

334
00:24:47,777 --> 00:24:49,613
I can feel the power surging within me.

335
00:24:50,530 --> 00:24:51,615
Good, good.

336
00:24:52,449 --> 00:24:53,867
However, Great Shogun,

337
00:24:54,659 --> 00:24:56,369
if he's a concern,

338
00:24:56,453 --> 00:24:58,705
why not simply kill him?

339
00:24:59,915 --> 00:25:04,461
But then, it would all end there.

340
00:25:10,634 --> 00:25:11,843
Take his land,

341
00:25:13,428 --> 00:25:14,638
strip him of his power,

342
00:25:15,805 --> 00:25:17,474
and let him do nothing

343
00:25:17,557 --> 00:25:18,850
but grow old.

344
00:25:21,061 --> 00:25:22,270
For a samurai,

345
00:25:23,104 --> 00:25:26,316
that is the most
humiliating punishment of all.

346
00:25:31,613 --> 00:25:32,739
So it failed.

347
00:25:32,822 --> 00:25:35,617
Let's lower the dose
of poison nut next time.

348
00:25:36,618 --> 00:25:37,661
Right.

349
00:25:43,625 --> 00:25:45,335
Where did he go?

350
00:25:45,418 --> 00:25:47,879
There he is! The thief!

351
00:25:51,216 --> 00:25:52,842
What a haul!

352
00:25:54,928 --> 00:25:56,846
Kagemaru! Kill him!

353
00:25:58,348 --> 00:25:59,307
Kagemaru?!

354
00:26:00,183 --> 00:26:01,184
Sasuke?

355
00:26:05,146 --> 00:26:09,067
You used to be a village thug.
How'd you end up as a bodyguard?

356
00:26:11,569 --> 00:26:13,029
I gave up stealing.

357
00:26:14,072 --> 00:26:15,657
-What?
-Not only that.

358
00:26:16,658 --> 00:26:18,410
My fighting skills were recognized,

359
00:26:19,327 --> 00:26:21,162
and now I serve Lord Tokugawa.

360
00:26:22,372 --> 00:26:24,791
Tokugawa… You mean the Tokugawa clan?

361
00:26:25,417 --> 00:26:26,584
That's right.

362
00:26:26,668 --> 00:26:29,296
They're hiring lots of ninjas now.

363
00:26:30,922 --> 00:26:33,842
The Tokugawa will rule Japan from now on.

364
00:26:35,176 --> 00:26:36,761
My mom's so proud of me.

365
00:26:38,596 --> 00:26:42,350
You should quit this nonsense
and get an honest job.

366
00:26:43,059 --> 00:26:44,311
Make your parents proud.

367
00:26:45,729 --> 00:26:47,856
I don't have any parents.

368
00:26:50,233 --> 00:26:51,651
Old man Hakuunsai…

369
00:26:52,444 --> 00:26:54,070
He's been looking for you all this time.

370
00:27:01,536 --> 00:27:02,746
<i>He's getting old, after all.</i>

371
00:27:04,331 --> 00:27:06,458
He's probably planning
to leave the kids in your care.

372
00:27:12,047 --> 00:27:13,548
I'm taking this back.

373
00:27:18,136 --> 00:27:19,971
What's that pouch in your pocket?

374
00:27:22,640 --> 00:27:23,475
Well…

375
00:27:25,560 --> 00:27:26,853
It's the old man's.

376
00:27:28,229 --> 00:27:29,689
Come on.

377
00:27:29,773 --> 00:27:32,150
There's probably
nothing valuable in it, anyway.

378
00:27:41,034 --> 00:27:43,370
BOW BEFORE WHAT IS RIGHT
AND CURB YOUR PRIDE

379
00:27:43,453 --> 00:27:47,874
"Use your power for the good of all."

380
00:28:22,033 --> 00:28:23,701
Look, you messed up again. You suck.

381
00:28:23,785 --> 00:28:25,620
Just one more time! Just one more!

382
00:28:25,703 --> 00:28:27,664
-Let me have a turn.
-Please!

383
00:28:29,707 --> 00:28:31,042
-Amazing!
-Amazing!

384
00:28:32,335 --> 00:28:33,628
-Sasuke!
-Sasuke!

385
00:28:34,712 --> 00:28:37,757
Hey. Are you guys training properly?

386
00:28:38,842 --> 00:28:41,219
Guess I'll have to step in and coach you.

387
00:28:49,269 --> 00:28:51,312
You're back, Sasuke?

388
00:28:57,318 --> 00:28:58,611
So you're Hakuunsai.

389
00:29:03,950 --> 00:29:05,326
Serve the Tokugawa.

390
00:29:05,410 --> 00:29:06,369
HATTORI HANZO

391
00:29:07,203 --> 00:29:08,163
Hattori…

392
00:29:10,206 --> 00:29:11,166
Hanzo.

393
00:29:24,095 --> 00:29:25,013
Old man!

394
00:29:25,096 --> 00:29:26,264
What the hell?!

395
00:29:26,347 --> 00:29:28,099
Sasuke, run…

396
00:29:29,476 --> 00:29:31,269
Take the children!

397
00:29:31,978 --> 00:29:32,896
You there.

398
00:29:33,480 --> 00:29:36,232
You're the thief
who escaped the execution grounds.

399
00:29:37,275 --> 00:29:39,194
Thanks to you, I found his whereabouts.

400
00:29:39,903 --> 00:29:40,904
I owe you one.

401
00:29:41,488 --> 00:29:43,406
You bastard!

402
00:29:46,701 --> 00:29:48,578
Lord Hakuunsai!

403
00:29:52,457 --> 00:29:57,587
Conceal, Secure, Bind, Switch!

404
00:30:02,509 --> 00:30:03,426
Old man!

405
00:30:10,308 --> 00:30:11,142
Old man!

406
00:30:13,019 --> 00:30:15,480
You bastard…

407
00:30:16,773 --> 00:30:19,234
I'll make you pay!

408
00:30:30,203 --> 00:30:31,120
Old man.

409
00:30:33,915 --> 00:30:34,916
That technique

410
00:30:35,583 --> 00:30:36,584
just now…

411
00:30:37,627 --> 00:30:38,670
I don't know.

412
00:30:46,052 --> 00:30:47,262
It was…

413
00:30:48,555 --> 00:30:49,597
Clone.

414
00:30:58,439 --> 00:30:59,440
Sasuke…

415
00:31:00,900 --> 00:31:01,860
What?

416
00:31:12,161 --> 00:31:13,246
Go to…

417
00:31:14,163 --> 00:31:14,998
Kudoyama.

418
00:31:16,708 --> 00:31:17,625
Kudoyama?

419
00:31:24,674 --> 00:31:25,758
There…

420
00:31:26,718 --> 00:31:27,969
There…

421
00:31:40,815 --> 00:31:41,816
Hey…

422
00:31:43,026 --> 00:31:44,027
Hey, old man!

423
00:31:45,194 --> 00:31:46,446
Old man!

424
00:31:46,529 --> 00:31:49,365
Hang in there, old man! Hey!

425
00:31:50,074 --> 00:31:51,200
Hey!

426
00:31:54,245 --> 00:31:56,789
What did the old man ever do to you?!

427
00:31:57,749 --> 00:31:58,666
Hey!

428
00:32:04,797 --> 00:32:06,925
You bastard…

429
00:32:09,844 --> 00:32:10,678
Enchain.

430
00:32:10,762 --> 00:32:11,596
ENCHAIN

431
00:32:15,475 --> 00:32:17,435
You want to know what he did?

432
00:32:19,270 --> 00:32:20,355
I'll tell you.

433
00:32:22,190 --> 00:32:25,401
He rejected
the Great Elder's generous offer,

434
00:32:27,403 --> 00:32:28,988
and chose the Sanada instead.

435
00:32:34,077 --> 00:32:36,496
All for some foolish loyalty.

436
00:32:44,253 --> 00:32:47,382
Ninjas are the source
of the Tokugawa's power!

437
00:32:48,633 --> 00:32:51,594
You will support this nation
from the shadows!

438
00:32:52,387 --> 00:32:53,429
Yes, sir!

439
00:32:53,513 --> 00:32:55,515
Simply obey your orders.

440
00:32:56,265 --> 00:32:57,517
Yes, sir!

441
00:32:57,600 --> 00:32:58,643
Jump!

442
00:33:00,478 --> 00:33:02,355
I said jump.

443
00:33:21,124 --> 00:33:22,041
Mom…

444
00:33:23,918 --> 00:33:24,752
Mom…

445
00:33:25,378 --> 00:33:26,379
I'm sorry!

446
00:33:42,145 --> 00:33:43,813
Not a single one left, eh?

447
00:33:49,652 --> 00:33:52,238
Not even a ninja who can fly?

448
00:33:54,282 --> 00:33:55,616
A flying ninja…

449
00:33:56,784 --> 00:33:57,827
How marvelous.

450
00:34:03,207 --> 00:34:04,333
What of Hakuunsai?

451
00:34:06,544 --> 00:34:07,587
I cut him down.

452
00:34:08,171 --> 00:34:09,338
I see.

453
00:34:11,507 --> 00:34:13,426
Yukimura and Hakuunsai…

454
00:34:14,886 --> 00:34:17,430
Now we have nothing to fear
from behind us.

455
00:34:55,134 --> 00:34:56,469
It's all my fault.

456
00:35:18,324 --> 00:35:19,909
Kudoyama…

457
00:35:23,704 --> 00:35:24,789
Okuni!

458
00:35:25,706 --> 00:35:28,167
-You're back, Okuni.
-Sorry to keep you waiting.

459
00:35:28,793 --> 00:35:30,086
Well? How did it go?

460
00:35:30,169 --> 00:35:32,338
I was sure this batch would sell well.

461
00:35:32,421 --> 00:35:34,382
As you can see, they're all sold out.

462
00:35:35,466 --> 00:35:39,303
The unbreakable Sanada cords
are gaining fame across the land.

463
00:35:40,263 --> 00:35:42,473
Here's the payment,
and what you asked for.

464
00:35:43,141 --> 00:35:44,267
This is a great help.

465
00:35:47,186 --> 00:35:48,020
All right.

466
00:35:52,567 --> 00:35:53,734
That's a lot.

467
00:35:53,818 --> 00:35:55,695
This should keep us fed for a while.

468
00:35:56,279 --> 00:35:57,780
We're deeply grateful!

469
00:35:58,739 --> 00:35:59,699
Thank Okuni.

470
00:36:00,324 --> 00:36:03,536
The Sanada cord
has become fairly well-known by now.

471
00:36:04,871 --> 00:36:06,289
I'll teach everyone how to make it.

472
00:36:07,039 --> 00:36:08,708
I hope it'll help you all make a living.

473
00:36:09,417 --> 00:36:11,460
Lord Yukimura, let's play tag!

474
00:36:11,544 --> 00:36:12,753
Let's play tag!

475
00:36:12,837 --> 00:36:13,838
All right.

476
00:36:15,798 --> 00:36:17,675
No matter how dire the situation,

477
00:36:17,758 --> 00:36:19,510
there's always a way
to turn things around.

478
00:36:20,553 --> 00:36:24,140
But… how do you manage
to weave so many cords?

479
00:36:29,520 --> 00:36:30,521
As expected of our lord.

480
00:36:31,647 --> 00:36:33,399
Well? What do you think, Unno?

481
00:36:34,483 --> 00:36:37,737
I'll have you know
I never doubted our lord for a second.

482
00:36:38,988 --> 00:36:42,867
And who was it that said he'd gone soft?

483
00:36:42,950 --> 00:36:44,952
I was just venting!

484
00:36:45,912 --> 00:36:48,956
It's paid off, all the hard work
we've put into improving the Sanada cords.

485
00:36:49,540 --> 00:36:52,210
Well, my brother did most of the work.

486
00:36:52,919 --> 00:36:55,796
All right! Number 2053.

487
00:36:58,966 --> 00:37:00,176
That's enough!

488
00:37:00,927 --> 00:37:03,804
What are you lot doing? Hey!

489
00:37:04,805 --> 00:37:07,016
What's all this money?!

490
00:37:07,683 --> 00:37:09,936
I have good news for you.

491
00:37:10,728 --> 00:37:15,524
The rice allowance granted to the Sanada
by the Great Elder

492
00:37:17,151 --> 00:37:19,153
will be cut by half starting next season.

493
00:37:20,029 --> 00:37:24,617
"Keep the common folk alive,
but not well enough to live."

494
00:37:25,534 --> 00:37:27,286
Those are the Great Elder's orders.

495
00:37:28,454 --> 00:37:30,039
The common folk!

496
00:37:30,706 --> 00:37:34,377
Keep them alive,
but not well enough to live.

497
00:37:34,460 --> 00:37:35,461
Bastards…

498
00:37:44,845 --> 00:37:46,806
It's all thanks to you. Have a drink.

499
00:37:53,729 --> 00:37:56,190
If we're going to deal with him,
let me do it.

500
00:37:56,274 --> 00:37:59,944
-No, poison would be more certain.
-Don't act rashly!

501
00:38:00,027 --> 00:38:03,197
If the checkpoint magistrate dies,
Lord Yukimura will be the prime suspect.

502
00:38:04,865 --> 00:38:08,077
But if they cut
our rice allowance any further…

503
00:38:08,160 --> 00:38:10,121
Don't worry about me.

504
00:38:10,621 --> 00:38:12,039
Even so…

505
00:38:12,123 --> 00:38:14,834
You've been giving rice
to the poor villagers,

506
00:38:14,917 --> 00:38:17,253
and you're barely eating yourself,
aren't you?

507
00:38:17,336 --> 00:38:19,046
My presence…

508
00:38:19,672 --> 00:38:22,174
is a burden on this village.

509
00:38:23,509 --> 00:38:24,635
That's the least I could do.

510
00:38:24,719 --> 00:38:26,262
We'll have to leave the village, then.

511
00:38:27,305 --> 00:38:29,056
There must be a way if we just try.

512
00:38:30,016 --> 00:38:31,934
Have you forgotten about that thief

513
00:38:32,560 --> 00:38:35,563
who came to this village the other day?

514
00:38:52,747 --> 00:38:54,248
But if things go on like this…

515
00:38:57,084 --> 00:38:58,377
We're still missing…

516
00:39:00,129 --> 00:39:01,213
one last piece.

517
00:39:22,526 --> 00:39:24,945
Botched the landing again.

518
00:39:28,824 --> 00:39:30,910
So this is Kudoyama, huh?

519
00:39:35,831 --> 00:39:36,791
Hey, you.

520
00:39:38,793 --> 00:39:40,711
Recognize this <i>shuriken?</i>

521
00:39:47,802 --> 00:39:48,719
Are you all right?

522
00:39:49,637 --> 00:39:50,471
Yeah.

523
00:39:55,810 --> 00:39:57,228
It's the same design.

524
00:40:00,940 --> 00:40:02,316
So it was you lot!

525
00:40:17,540 --> 00:40:18,749
You're as good as Saizo.

526
00:40:28,008 --> 00:40:31,137
You're the ones who killed the old man!

527
00:40:39,937 --> 00:40:43,065
Shield, Secure, Surge…

528
00:40:45,317 --> 00:40:46,819
Mist Concealment.

529
00:40:46,902 --> 00:40:48,028
MIST CONCEALMENT

530
00:41:09,216 --> 00:41:12,386
BOMB

531
00:41:12,970 --> 00:41:14,138
Let go of me.

532
00:41:24,690 --> 00:41:27,401
-Are you all in cahoots?
-Yeah.

533
00:41:29,570 --> 00:41:30,613
Looking for this?

534
00:41:31,655 --> 00:41:33,657
I took it for safekeeping. It's dangerous.

535
00:41:34,408 --> 00:41:36,827
What kind of behavior is that,
attacking us out of nowhere?

536
00:41:36,911 --> 00:41:39,288
What ninja clan are you from?

537
00:41:39,371 --> 00:41:41,248
Now that you've seen us,
we have to kill you.

538
00:41:41,332 --> 00:41:42,333
Shall we?

539
00:41:44,210 --> 00:41:45,419
Double sixes.

540
00:41:45,503 --> 00:41:47,213
Now that's a roll.

541
00:41:47,296 --> 00:41:48,923
Then let's proceed at once.

542
00:41:49,006 --> 00:41:50,007
Wait.

543
00:42:01,143 --> 00:42:02,311
Where did you get this?

544
00:42:04,939 --> 00:42:05,898
It's a keepsake.

545
00:42:06,524 --> 00:42:07,858
From the old man who died.

546
00:42:09,151 --> 00:42:10,236
Was this old man…

547
00:42:11,070 --> 00:42:12,655
Hakuunsai?

548
00:42:14,114 --> 00:42:15,074
Yeah.

549
00:42:16,242 --> 00:42:17,326
I see.

550
00:42:18,410 --> 00:42:19,745
So he's passed away.

551
00:42:21,664 --> 00:42:22,581
What's your name?

552
00:42:23,791 --> 00:42:24,917
Sasuke.

553
00:42:25,793 --> 00:42:27,628
I'm sorry we treated you so roughly.

554
00:42:27,711 --> 00:42:30,256
Everyone, put away your weapons.

555
00:42:30,339 --> 00:42:31,340
Yes, sir.

556
00:42:36,136 --> 00:42:37,846
I'm Sanada Yukimura.

557
00:42:38,973 --> 00:42:41,267
I knew Hakuunsai well.

558
00:42:41,350 --> 00:42:42,476
Sanada?

559
00:42:45,729 --> 00:42:48,774
So you're the famous Sanada Braves?

560
00:42:50,401 --> 00:42:52,945
You're nothing like what I'd heard.

561
00:42:53,028 --> 00:42:54,822
What do you mean by that?

562
00:42:56,156 --> 00:42:59,994
Then why are you using the same <i>shuriken</i>
as the ninja who killed the old man?

563
00:43:00,661 --> 00:43:02,079
Acting all high and mighty.

564
00:43:03,789 --> 00:43:06,333
The one who killed Hakuunsai
was most likely…

565
00:43:09,086 --> 00:43:10,296
Hattori Hanzo.

566
00:43:12,131 --> 00:43:13,424
Hattori Hanzo?

567
00:43:13,507 --> 00:43:17,469
The head ninja of the Tokugawa clan.
The greatest ninja in all of Japan.

568
00:43:17,553 --> 00:43:21,974
Saizo hails from the same Iga clan.

569
00:43:24,351 --> 00:43:26,270
Hattori Hanzo…

570
00:43:29,148 --> 00:43:30,649
I'll kill him.

571
00:43:31,775 --> 00:43:32,860
The one who gave the order

572
00:43:33,902 --> 00:43:35,112
was Tokugawa Ieyasu.

573
00:43:36,447 --> 00:43:38,449
Then I'll kill them both!

574
00:43:51,420 --> 00:43:53,547
You came back with a companion.

575
00:43:56,425 --> 00:43:57,301
Sasuke.

576
00:43:58,052 --> 00:44:00,346
We share the same goal.

577
00:44:01,430 --> 00:44:02,473
What do you mean?

578
00:44:03,223 --> 00:44:06,602
We're after Ieyasu's head, too.

579
00:44:06,685 --> 00:44:10,064
My lord, we can't trust someone
whose background we don't even know.

580
00:44:13,192 --> 00:44:14,443
Will you fight alongside us?

581
00:44:14,985 --> 00:44:16,445
Against the whole realm.

582
00:44:30,250 --> 00:44:31,835
Don't mess with me!

583
00:44:31,919 --> 00:44:34,171
Like hell I'll become your lackey.

584
00:44:34,254 --> 00:44:37,424
The old man died because of you.

585
00:44:37,508 --> 00:44:39,385
He chose the Sanada over the Tokugawa!

586
00:44:41,136 --> 00:44:43,180
That was a fine display of loyalty.

587
00:44:43,263 --> 00:44:45,099
What? Loyalty?

588
00:44:45,724 --> 00:44:47,476
To hell with that!

589
00:44:48,060 --> 00:44:50,020
That's enough, you bastard.

590
00:44:50,938 --> 00:44:52,731
I don't trust anyone.

591
00:44:56,652 --> 00:44:59,488
Will you put your skills to use for us?

592
00:45:08,705 --> 00:45:12,543
There was one piece missing,
one we absolutely needed.

593
00:45:14,294 --> 00:45:15,170
And now,

594
00:45:15,963 --> 00:45:17,589
it falls right out of the sky.

595
00:45:19,049 --> 00:45:19,967
What?

596
00:45:23,011 --> 00:45:25,139
Damn, I'm bleeding too much.

597
00:45:26,515 --> 00:45:27,433
Oh, he fell.

598
00:45:31,353 --> 00:45:32,354
We've been spotted.

599
00:45:32,438 --> 00:45:34,189
Hey, isn't that bad?

600
00:45:35,232 --> 00:45:38,026
Could someone… bring him here?

601
00:45:41,905 --> 00:45:44,366
Sorry to keep you waiting, everyone.

602
00:45:45,868 --> 00:45:46,994
We're leaving this village.

603
00:45:54,042 --> 00:45:56,670
We're taking down the Tokugawa.

604
00:46:28,952 --> 00:46:30,996
Subtitle translation by: Sayo Takada

605
00:46:31,079 --> 00:46:33,916
THIS DRAMA IS A WORK OF FICTION
